1
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,380
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa

2
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:23,520
I kicked a pebble and sent it flying far

3
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:29,360
Joking around with the gym teacher, Kashiwa

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,760
They laughed at me for staying so cheerful

5
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:37,400
Even if I somehow stir up some energy

6
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,660
Gutsy, there's a reason

7
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:41,000
The same nightmare, unchanged

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,840
The streets are gentler now

9
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:46,980
Because the crows are cawing

10
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:48,840
Coffee is what gives it to us, isn't it

11
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:53,860
Yakitori, is it really true?

12
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,480
Of the pointed hat

13
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:04,040
From the waterworks to the Oishi line,
the sun sets

14
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:10,040
Tomorrow it'll end the same way,
dropped and finished

15
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:12,660
Gutsy-gutsy, yeah, happiness again

16
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:16,260
Because I'm a fool who took the
easy way and only realized it later

17
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:26,880
Koi Panic!

18
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:36,360
What a magnificent nishikigoi.

19
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:38,360
Get it?

20
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:43,200
That... the little pearl sheen on it is nice,
isn't it?

21
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,160
Yes, they're really beautiful.

22
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:52,300
The three-colored ones are lovely too, aren't they?
Let me see... hey, stop that! The water's...

23
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:59,160
Aaaaah! It's all right now,
I've gotten rid of the germs.

24
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:06,220
Oh well... even the pets have come to this.
Sorry, when it comes to nishikigoi...

25
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:13,360
I get so carried away, like a child, don't I?
It's no wonder, you've raised them with care since they were fry.

26
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,900
after all, you've been raising
them since they were young.

27
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:15,700
Really?

28
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:18,520
I thought all nishikigoi looked the same,

29
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:21,260
but they really come in all sorts of patterns,
don't they?

30
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:22,480
Right?

31
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,880
Even though they're all
just called nishikigoi,

32
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:27,100
there's Wagoi, and there's Doitsugoi too.

33
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:28,200
Doitsugoi?

34
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:29,780
Koi were improved through breeding,

35
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:32,960
and it was Japan that made them into
the beautiful nishikigoi we see today.

36
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:35,720
In Asia, America, and Europe alike,

37
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:37,720
there are plenty of nishikigoi enthusiasts.

38
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:40,860
Today I called you all here

39
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:43,480
because I wanted you
to see these nishikigoi.

40
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:46,080
What, you went to all
this trouble just for that?

41
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:47,640
What do you mean, "what"?

42
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:50,900
Someone as worthless as
you wouldn't understand,

43
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:51,540
but look.

44
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:54,960
That koi is a whopping 53 centimeters long,

45
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:57,860
the one I plan to enter
in the next competition.

46
00:02:57,860 --> 00:02:59,780
A competition for nishikigoi?

47
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:00,480
Yeah.

48
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:03,180
No grand champion has been awarded in years,

49
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:07,940
so just being selected is a great
honor for nishikigoi enthusiasts.

50
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:12,400
As it grows, its pattern changes too,

51
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,440
and this one has settled into a good look.

52
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,400
Male, three-color Taisho, right?

53
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,980
W-what? Why are you here?

54
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:20,680
Do you know him, Yo-chan?

55
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:21,820
Of course I do.

56
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:26,640
I'm the one who takes care of the
88 nishikigoi kept at Matoi's house.

57
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:27,840
You, senpai?

58
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:30,760
Now that you mention it,
you're good at raising things.

59
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:35,540
Well, with nishikigoi, creating the right environment,
like water quality and filtration, is what matters.

60
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:36,580
Hey, Chief.

61
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:39,360
Yes, yes, that's right.

62
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:43,760
Go on, swim over there with everyone,
Koi Jirō.

63
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,780
Koi Jirō.

64
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:48,200
Yeah, I named him after Dai-jirō,
from my own name.

65
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:51,160
They're all like my children, you know.

66
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:56,820
Chief, this pond has a lot of trees and grass,
so garbage builds up easily.

67
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:59,040
Unless we stop the water and drain it,

68
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:00,200
What?

69
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:06,360
the poor water flow in the pond breeds
pathogens like anchor worms and fish lice.

70
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:10,240
Amazing, Ryotsu,
I didn't know you knew this much.

71
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:13,940
White spot disease occurs when the
water temperature suddenly drops.

72
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:20,100
Raise the water temperature to about 28 degrees and mix in about 1% salt,
and they'll recover.

73
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:25,860
With a koi like that, you could aim
for the championship, don't you think?

74
00:04:25,860 --> 00:04:29,380
That's right, Chief.
You're confident, aren't you?

75
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:33,340
Well, I think it has a fair shot.

76
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:35,462
What worries me is the next four days,
starting tomorrow,

77
00:04:35,512 --> 00:04:38,020
when my wife and I go off on a trip.

78
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:41,400
It's to make up for not doing anything
for our silver wedding anniversary.

79
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,940
So I'm wondering what to do in the meantime.

80
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:48,320
Then why not leave them at
our pet management center?

81
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:51,260
We'll thoroughly check everything,
from the water quality on.

82
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:53,780
Is there such a thing?

83
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:57,460
The management fee is 50,000 yen a day,
so it's a bit pricey.

84
00:04:57,980 --> 00:04:58,920
50,000 yen?

85
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:04,800
Just taking care of them is enough.
You can't put a price on that, after all.

86
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:11,400
Fine, I'll leave it to you. What's with the shouting,
Ryotsu? Don't be so distant.

87
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:19,580
Leave it to this place, 30,000 a day. Or rather,
I'll take the best care of them. You, but...

88
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:28,220
I breed the nishikigoi at Matoi's house and raise them from fry.
What, of course I'd never...

89
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:34,480
That's what you say, but you're
just planning to make money off it.

90
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:43,740
Your eyes lit up the moment you heard 50,000 a day.
You have to treat koi with love above all else.

91
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:49,380
Indeed.
A man who is in love with koi is truly...

92
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:55,080
Alright, I understand.
I'm counting on you, Ryotsu. Leave it to me.

93
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:03,220
10,000 yen a day, 40,000 yen for four days.

94
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:07,640
Ryotsu, please take extra good
care of Koike Jiro and the others.

95
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:10,020
Rest easy, as if you're on a great big ship.

96
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:11,900
You're going by plane, aren't you?

97
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:15,320
Then rest easy, as if you're riding a flying saucer.
Leave it to me.

98
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:18,760
I'm not joking, I'm counting on you.

99
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:19,600
See you.

100
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:20,920
Well then, thanks in advance.

101
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,500
Have a safe trip.

102
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:26,260
Bring back a souvenir, will you?

103
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:31,060
Just feeding them and getting 10,000 yen a day,
what a sweet deal.

104
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:34,680
Go on, eat that.

105
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:37,820
Koike Rō, Koike Satoshi, Koike Taira, Koita.

106
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:45,220
Still, I'm bored.

107
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:51,120
Guess I'll teach them
some tricks to kill time.

108
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,680
Everyone, gather round!

109
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:59,920
Alright, let's see who can jump the highest.
It's a race!

110
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:03,100
I'll give this to the winner.

111
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:05,800
Like carp could ever understand love, right?

112
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:09,980
Koishi.

113
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:14,240
This one's smarter than the others.

114
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:16,680
Guess I'll train this one properly.

115
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:20,320
Here we go, 1, 2, 3!

116
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,140
Alright, next is hoop jumping!

117
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:31,900
Alright.

118
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:34,420
If I train this one properly...

119
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:36,800
I might actually make some money off it.

120
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:51,920
Just kidding.

121
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,500
Hey, let's go!

122
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:06,920
Where are you going?

123
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:10,860
Wait up!

124
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:35,260


125
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,760
Taaake!

126
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:41,000
Ow

127
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,120
Hey, are you alright?

128
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:45,040
Ow!

129
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:48,360
Whoa!

130
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,840
Stop that truck!

131
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:56,300
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

132
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,780
There are too few
traffic lights to catch up!

133
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:01,200
Hey!

134
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:03,380
I'm borrowing this!

135
00:09:03,380 --> 00:09:05,600
Wait, wait, wait!

136
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:17,420
Wait, wait!

137
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:30,140
Koichiro, are you okay?

138
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:53,680
Koijiro! Koijiro! Come back! Koijiro!

139
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:56,500
Koijiro!

140
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:03,120
Koijiro's...

141
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:05,880
Shh! If Reiko finds out, we're in trouble!

142
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:10,040
B-but what are you planning to do?

143
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:13,800
That koi is the one the
Chief doted on the most, right?

144
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,820
The one that was supposed to be
entered in the koi competition...

145
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:17,793
So you're in a bind.

146
00:10:17,843 --> 00:10:20,623
Since every one of the 100
koi has a different pattern,

147
00:10:20,673 --> 00:10:22,720
we can't just pass off a look-alike.

148
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:25,220
So, come here and lend me your ear.

149
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:31,180
A robotic fish developed by
Nakagawa's Electro Division?!

150
00:10:31,180 --> 00:10:31,940
Shee!

151
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:39,491
Here's a photo of Koijiro.

152
00:10:39,541 --> 00:10:42,208
We'll make a lookalike shell out of latex,

153
00:10:42,258 --> 00:10:44,220
and hide that mechanism inside it.

154
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:47,080
You're going to build a robot koi?

155
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,660
What are you two talking about?

156
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:50,760
Snap!

157
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:52,950
It's nothing.

158
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,040
Just man talk. Right, Nakagawa?

159
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:56,060
Oh, yes.

160
00:10:57,180 --> 00:10:59,020
Let's go over there and talk some more.

161
00:10:59,080 --> 00:10:59,480
Right, right.

162
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:03,779
Good. The movements look so real,

163
00:11:03,829 --> 00:11:06,720
the motor noise is quiet too.
It's no different from the real thing.

164
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:09,776
Fish don't have facial expressions,
after all.

165
00:11:09,826 --> 00:11:12,000
But tomorrow's competition...

166
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,540
I can only pray it gets
knocked out in the preliminaries.

167
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:15,820
I'm home.

168
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:16,960
I'm back.

169
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:21,600
Ryotsu, was Koijiro doing well?

170
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:22,940
Of course.

171
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:24,940
Koijiro.

172
00:11:24,940 --> 00:11:27,420
Ryotsu.

173
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:30,080
Good work.

174
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:31,760
His color is good too, and he looks healthy.

175
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:35,100
At this rate,
he should do well in the competition too.

176
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:38,360
Yes, I'll be going along with him too.

177
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:40,580
I'm looking forward to tomorrow.

178
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:59,360
If they're real connoisseurs,
they'll see through the fake.

179
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:01,880
I hope they get knocked out
in the preliminaries quickly.

180
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:03,860
Ryotsu! Nakagawa!

181
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:07,520
We made it through the preliminaries!

182
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:08,720
What?

183
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:12,300
What, is it a bad thing that we advanced?

184
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:14,740
No, no, not at all. That's great news.

185
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:19,880
That's odd. It suddenly stopped moving.

186
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:24,400
Koijiro, what's wrong? Koijiro! Koijiro!

187
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,940
It's out of battery, senpai.

188
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:30,280
What?! Excuse me...

189
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:32,740
What are you planning to do, Ryotsu?

190
00:12:32,740 --> 00:12:33,660
Nakagawa.

191
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:34,140
Yes.

192
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:34,240
Yes!

193
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:38,620
Koijiro!

194
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,180
Leave it to me!

195
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:42,160
Koijiro...

196
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:48,180
At this rate,
the battery's going to die again soon...

197
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:49,960
Senpai, hurry, hurry!

198
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,220
I know, I know!

199
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,500
I'll just modify it a little.

200
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:56,680
Koijiro... Koijiro...

201
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:57,520
Sorry to keep you waiting!

202
00:12:58,280 --> 00:12:59,400
O-okay!

203
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:01,580
Koijiro is perfectly fine, just like this!

204
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:09,780
Aaaaaaah!

205
00:13:09,780 --> 00:13:11,820
Aaaaaaah!

206
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:14,240
Aaaaaaah!

207
00:13:15,660 --> 00:13:16,700
Koijiro!

208
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:18,420
It's all right now.

209
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:22,600
We did it!

210
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:25,320
Koijiro made it to the final round!

211
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:25,780
Hey.

212
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:29,560
If it actually wins the whole thing,
we won't be able to cover this up anymore.

213
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:30,980
Eeeeeeeeh!

214
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:47,760
This is wonderful. Not only elegant and beautiful, it has such an active, lively presence.
Ace... really? Isn't it a little too energetic?

215
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:54,540
No, it has a dynamic vitality unlike any before.
It's fresh... but isn't it a bit overweight?

216
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:56,422
Amateurs may not understand,

217
00:13:56,472 --> 00:13:59,000
but this sense of volume is excellent.

218
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,720
W-well, no but...

219
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:02,340
Why are you nitpicking?

220
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,240
No, nothing.

221
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:06,020
I take it everyone agrees?

222
00:14:06,460 --> 00:14:07,260
No objections!

223
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:11,340
That's decided!
The winner is number 52, Taishō Sanshoku!

224
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:12,200
We did it!

225
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:12,540
What?!

226
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:14,500
Koijiro wins!

227
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,240
Senpai...

228
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:18,120
What an unexpected turn of events.

229
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:23,280
W-what?

230
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:27,740
Maybe the forced
modifications caught up with it.

231
00:14:37,660 --> 00:14:41,180
Whoa, I'm stunned!

232
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:44,480
What on earth is going on, Joes?

233
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:45,960
Hey, Yanos-san's

234
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:47,600
Koijiro?

235
00:14:55,820 --> 00:14:57,360
What is this, Ryotsu?

236
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:59,646
Also

237
00:14:59,696 --> 00:15:01,740
that, the robot...

238
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:06,880
A robot?! Where's the real Koijiro?

239
00:15:07,020 --> 00:15:10,200
He's probably living happily
out in the wild by now.

240
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:13,760
You idiot!

241
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:19,660
Damn it! I can't let it end like this!

242
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,420
In that case,
it's a rematch with the nishikigoi!

243
00:15:22,420 --> 00:15:24,980
We'll be back after the commercial break!

244
00:15:26,640 --> 00:15:28,080
What's Ryotsu up to?

245
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:29,680
He's been off work for ages, right?

246
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:31,540
It's not like he's sick.

247
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:35,140
Apparently he's secretly
started something new again.

248
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:36,900
Probably some way to make money.

249
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:39,980
Whatever. I don't know what he's doing.

250
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:43,080
If I don't have to see that guy's face,
I'll be glad to go home.

251
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:00,000
It's c-cold!

252
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:05,700
Whoa!

253
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:13,640
Why are there nishikigoi in the bath!

254
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,480
What are you doing, Mom!

255
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:17,020
That's harsh...

256
00:16:17,020 --> 00:16:18,940
That's cruel, senpai.

257
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:21,820
The dorm bath is off-limits for a while.

258
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:23,260
That's so one-sided!

259
00:16:23,260 --> 00:16:24,800
What have you started?

260
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:26,560
We're raising nishikigoi.

261
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:28,480
The good ones sell for high prices,
you know.

262
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,780
Just watch.

263
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:33,260
With this tortoiseshell pattern,
unprecedented patterns and sizes,

264
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:35,320
and combined with incredible strength,

265
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:37,900
a super nishikigoi is about to be born!

266
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:40,180
Super nishikigoi!

267
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:44,840
Good, good, it's going well.

268
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,440
They're growing fast, aren't they?

269
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:51,580
Without any sleep, I can keep the
water temperature steady, you see.

270
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:55,540
The ones I've artificially crossbred with
various varieties are growing well too.

271
00:16:55,540 --> 00:16:58,180
But isn't this bathroom
too cramped for them?

272
00:16:58,540 --> 00:16:59,860
I've already got that covered.

273
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:02,900
I'm building a pond in the dorm courtyard.

274
00:17:02,900 --> 00:17:04,560
As expected, you work fast.

275
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:10,720
Twenty-four hours a day, no sleep, no rest,
crossbreeding all sorts of varieties nonstop,

276
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:13,080
I'm going to produce the perfect koi.

277
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:15,240
And then I'll be rich.

278
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:23,880
Right, ocean osmosis water,
hormone fluid, and stuff like that.

279
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:26,460
Let's add Mamushi Drink too.

280
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:29,580
What?

281
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,520
Ryotsu has perfected the gentleman's love!

282
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:36,560
Yes, apparently it's a
gentleman over one meter long.

283
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:39,500
There's a big announcement event today,
you know.

284
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:43,420
I can't believe it, in such a short time.

285
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,560
Senpai's power is going to be limitless,
you know.

286
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:03,000
Everyone, the reason I've gathered
you here today is none other than

287
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,940
the ultimate koi that
mankind has been seeking.

288
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:07,980
That has finally been born.

289
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:29,400
I've never seen such a
powerful tricolor before.

290
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:33,480
No, it's different from both Taishō
tricolors and Shōwa tricolors.

291
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:37,400
It's a four-color, not a tricolor!

292
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:42,300
That's right, this is the miracle I created through sleepless,
tireless effort.

293
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:44,600
We'll call it the Ryotsu Four-Color.

294
00:18:57,400 --> 00:18:58,620
Senbai!

295
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:02,200
I hear orders are pouring
in from all over the world.

296
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,280
Don't panic.

297
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:05,640
We knew this would happen.

298
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:07,920
This place is too small.

299
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:12,000
We're going to keep multiplying them!

300
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:18,160
One breeding yields 100,000 eggs that hatch.

301
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:21,140
The breeding power of the
Ryotsu Four-Color is no joke!

302
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:23,580
They say pets grow to resemble their owners,

303
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:26,200
and this koi is exactly like you, senpai.

304
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:27,320
Nahhahaha!

305
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:30,140
I've finally got my success story!

306
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:31,740
You did it, senpai!

307
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:35,320
These 300 are for Florida,

308
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:37,480
and these 500 are for Germany.

309
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:39,180
Keep shipping them out!

310
00:19:39,180 --> 00:19:40,540
Over there is Europe,

311
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:41,680
and over here is India.

312
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:45,380
The Middle East, Russia,
South America, China, Australia.

313
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:08,960
What?

314
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:13,380
Due to the nishikigoi with
a terrifying breeding power,

315
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:15,220
the Sumida River has been overrun.

316
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:18,600
This nishikigoi is called
the Ryotsu Four-Color,

317
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:22,640
and due to its short-tempered, violent nature,
it tips over its tank and escapes.

318
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:25,660
The owners, who couldn't stand
its outrageous selfishness,

319
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:28,540
dumped them in rivers and ponds,
and they've gone wild, it seems.

320
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:32,940
In rivers, lakes,
and park fountains across the country,

321
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:35,100
Ryotsu Four-Colors are breeding.

322
00:20:37,180 --> 00:20:38,780
What's going to happen, senpai?

323
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:41,780
I've got a bad feeling about this.

324
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:47,740
And the Seine has been completely
covered with Ryotsu Four-Colors!

325
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:02,280
We bring you the latest
footage from the Amazon River.

326
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:03,860
Please take a look.

327
00:21:03,860 --> 00:21:06,960
Ryotsu Four-Color koi are
reportedly chasing piranhas.

328
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:08,760
W-what's going on?

329
00:21:09,380 --> 00:21:13,600
The Ryotsu Four-Color is tough, and its
breeding power is incredible, after all.

330
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:17,220
It grows to fifty centimeters in three days,
you know.

331
00:21:17,220 --> 00:21:19,440
So, how long do they live?

332
00:21:20,140 --> 00:21:21,540
About five years, I think.

333
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:23,007
No,

334
00:21:23,057 --> 00:21:26,200
the average lifespan of a
brocade koi is seventy years.

335
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:28,480
Seventy years?!

336
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:31,660
If they keep multiplying at this rate...

337
00:21:33,280 --> 00:21:36,080
I don't want to imagine it,
I really don't want to!

338
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:47,100
Koijiro

339
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:50,060
Koijiro

340
00:21:50,060 --> 00:21:52,580
Koijiro

341
00:21:52,580 --> 00:22:08,880
Koijiro

342
00:22:17,660 --> 00:22:18,540
Koijiro

343
00:22:20,180 --> 00:22:21,160
Koijiro, is it?

344
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:25,700
Koijiro

345
00:22:32,380 --> 00:22:33,340
Koijiro

346
00:22:33,340 --> 00:22:35,920
You came back to us.

347
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:38,080
Koijiro

348
00:22:46,380 --> 00:22:48,620
Not just the Pacific and Atlantic,

349
00:22:48,620 --> 00:22:50,480
but also the South Pacific
and the Arctic Ocean,

350
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:53,100
large swarms of the Four-Color
koi have been confirmed.

351
00:22:53,780 --> 00:22:56,520
But for koi to cross the ocean like this!

352
00:22:56,520 --> 00:22:58,780
They're flying like flying fish!

353
00:22:58,780 --> 00:23:01,980
Come to think of it,
he also crossbred them with flying fish.

354
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:04,180
According to information from satellites,

355
00:23:04,180 --> 00:23:05,320
these swarms

356
00:23:05,320 --> 00:23:07,540
are all moving toward Japan.

357
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:09,540
Why Japan?

358
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:11,000
No way...

359
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:26,180
What do you mean, "no way"? Senpai!

360
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:28,240
We even crossbred them with salmon!

361
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:29,680
Well, then...

362
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:32,380
Just like salmon returning
to their birthplace,

363
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:35,580
they're heading back to Kameari!

364
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:42,060
They're coming back!

365
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:53,660
Well, look who it is!
Yoko from the tobacco shop!

366
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:56,360
The tomboy middle schooler
who threw me over her shoulder

367
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:58,480
has turned into a fine wife!

368
00:23:58,480 --> 00:23:59,900
You've changed so much I
almost didn't recognize you!

369
00:24:00,460 --> 00:24:03,120
Those days at the police box.

370
00:24:03,580 --> 00:24:05,860
Next time: "Police Box, A Little While Ago."

371
00:24:06,460 --> 00:24:07,000
Nice to see you.

372
00:24:11,860 --> 00:24:14,100
Surely on camera...

373
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:19,200
Everyone, come to our town!

374
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:20,840
Thank you!

